  "source_manifest_matches_final_tested_runtime": true,
  "architecture": [
    "Low EOT plus sentence FINAL is no longer a terminal false-interruption verdict.",
    "RESUME releases playback provisionally while the same candidate remains open for evidence; terminal ROLLBACK and CANCEL retain their ownership roles.",
    "Reuse existing speech merge grace for provisional playback hold, evidence deadline for bounded candidate continuation, candidate/generation identity, transcript assembler and timeout slot.",
    "Output cooldown controls repeated output actions, not whether evidence is received for an admitted active candidate.",
    "Pending semantic continuation can reuse the open candidate beyond the acoustic merge gap, within its existing evidence deadline; resolved/rejected candidates cannot reopen.",
    "Stable evidence timers survive provisional resume; weak followup HOLD schedules reevaluation through the existing timer.",
    "No phrase-specific rule, threshold reduction, new playback queue or SDK auto-interruption ownership change.",
    "Existing model-intent requests retain their pending-result wait; no new classifier or enabling of optional LLM provider."
  ],
  "automated_coverage": [
    "18 combinations: three Chinese/English topics, FINAL before/after VAD end, prefix/tail scores 0.003/0.424, 0.003/0.95 and 0.4/0.95.",
    "Late FINAL after output resumes, resumed speech inside/outside cooldown, long active speech exceeding playback budget, expiry with no continuation.",
    "Complete canonical text, exactly one continuation reply, no prefix-only commit, no premature resume during protected short pause, no stale candidate revival.",
    "Existing explicit preempt, unavailable/delayed intent model, PCM recovery, human speaking profiles and PTT contracts."
  ],
